@startuml
!theme plain
title M2 capability state and relay-only recovery

[*] --> Connecting
Connecting --> ConnectedFull : base TCP plus safe DNS plus validated relay
Connecting --> ConnectedDegraded : base TCP plus safe DNS, relay unavailable
Connecting --> Failed : mandatory TCP or safe DNS unavailable

ConnectedFull --> ConnectedDegraded : bootstrap, framing, health, process, or relay-lane failure
ConnectedFull --> Failed : mandatory base path or safe DNS failure
ConnectedDegraded --> RelayReprobe : recoverable relay reason and healthy base SSH
RelayReprobe --> ConnectedFull : fresh asset, identity, handshake, features, limits, health
RelayReprobe --> ConnectedDegraded : bounded attempt fails, retry remains eligible
RelayReprobe --> Failed : mandatory base path or safe DNS fails
ConnectedDegraded --> Failed : safe DNS or TCP becomes unusable

Connecting --> Stopping : provider stop
ConnectedFull --> Stopping : provider stop
ConnectedDegraded --> Stopping : provider stop
RelayReprobe --> Stopping : provider stop
Failed --> Stopping : provider stop
Stopping --> [*]

note right of ConnectedFull
TCP: usable
Safe DNS: usable
General UDP: relay only
end note

note right of ConnectedDegraded
TCP: usable
Safe DNS: tunneled fallback only
General UDP: explicitly rejected
No physical fallback
end note

note bottom of RelayReprobe
M2 owns relay-only reprobe on the healthy authenticated base transport.
M3 owns path, host, route, lane-pool, sleep, NAT64, and captive reconnect.
end note
@enduml